{"id": "xmoldova", "name": "Codru Nature Reserve (Codrii)", "short": "Codrii Reserve", "place": "Moldova", "lat": 47.1, "lon": 28.4, "side": "r", "cont": "Europe", "country": "Moldova", "kind": "Forest", "park": true, "blurb": "Oak and beech hill forest where martens, buzzards and dormice share a woodland web.", "tip": {"id": "beech", "title": "Remove the beech nuts", "text": "Set European beech to -100% and watch edible dormice, hawfinches, great tits and roe deer, then the marten and buzzard that hunt them."}, "sources": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Codru Reserve", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Codru_Reserve"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Codru (forest)", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Codru_(forest)"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: European pine marten", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/European_pine_marten"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Common buzzard", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_buzzard"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Great spotted woodpecker", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_spotted_woodpecker"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Grass snake", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grass_snake"}], "notes": "The species list comes from GBIF occurrence records inside a circle around the park, so it can include nearby areas. Feeding links come from GloBI records and the sources listed where they state them; others are general ecology and are illustrative.", "imgwiki": "Codru Reserve", "icon": "aspen", "tier": "overview", "nodes": [{"id": "sun", "sp": "sunlight", "xh": 0.1, "desc": "Light reaching the forest floor drives the spring herb layer and the growth of canopy leaves."}, {"id": "rain", "sp": "rainfall", "xh": 0.3, "desc": "Moldova has a dry continental climate, so rain and soil moisture set how well the hill forests grow."}, {"id": "soil", "sp": "forest soil and leaf litter", "xh": 0.55, "desc": "Fallen leaves and wood break down into the soil nutrients that the trees take up again."}, {"id": "decomp", "sp": "decomposer community", "xh": 0.88, "desc": "Break down leaf litter, dead wood and carcasses, returning nutrients to the soil."}, {"id": "oak", "sp": "quercus petraea", "xh": 0.12, "desc": "A broadleaf canopy tree of the hill forests. Its acorns, leaves and dead wood feed many animals.", "ic": "aspen", "badge": "Foundation species"}, {"id": "beech", "sp": "fagus sylvatica", "xh": 0.35, "desc": "A tall shade-casting canopy tree whose nuts are eaten by rodents, birds and deer.", "no": ["badge"]}, {"id": "hornbeam", "sp": "carpinus betulus", "xh": 0.58, "desc": "A common mid-canopy tree of Central European broadleaf forest that produces winged seeds."}, {"id": "cornel", "sp": "cornus mas", "xh": 0.82}, {"id": "stagbeetle", "sp": "lucanus cervus", "xh": 0.06}, {"id": "gallwasp", "sp": "cynips quercusfolii", "xh": 0.2}, {"id": "chafer", "sp": "cetonia aurata", "xh": 0.34}, {"id": "roedeer", "sp": "capreolus capreolus", "xh": 0.48, "desc": "A small deer that browses grass, leaves, berries and young shoots in woodland and edges."}, {"id": "dormouse", "sp": "glis glis", "xh": 0.62, "wiki": "Edible dormouse", "desc": "A tree-climbing rodent of broadleaf forest that eats nuts, seeds and fruit."}, {"id": "hawfinch", "sp": "coccothraustes coccothraustes", "xh": 0.76}, {"id": "greattit", "sp": "parus major", "xh": 0.9, "desc": "A cavity-nesting songbird that eats insects and seeds, including beech nuts."}, {"id": "shrew", "sp": "sorex araneus", "xh": 0.1}, {"id": "toad", "sp": "bufo bufo", "xh": 0.3}, {"id": "snake", "sp": "natrix natrix", "xh": 0.5, "name": "European grass snake", "desc": "A snake that hunts mainly amphibians, often at pond and stream edges."}, {"id": "woodpecker", "sp": "dendrocopos major", "xh": 0.7, "desc": "Digs beetle larvae from wood, eats tree seeds, and sometimes raids tit nests for eggs and chicks."}, {"id": "raven", "sp": "corvus corax", "xh": 0.9, "wiki": "Common raven", "desc": "A large omnivorous crow that scavenges carrion among other foods."}, {"id": "marten", "sp": "martes martes", "xh": 0